-- title:
--   Theorem 4.6 — MPGA is well defined: the line search terminates and the iterates stay in $\mathcal S$
-- statement:
--   Suppose Assumption 2 holds, and let $(x^{(t)},y^{(t)})$, with step sizes $\alpha_{(t)}$, be generated by MPGA with any index sequence and any memory $M$. Let $\mathcal S$ be built from a bound $\bar g_{\mathcal X}$ of $g$ on $\mathcal X$ and from $\underline\alpha$.
--
--   1. Step 2-X terminates in finitely many steps at some $\alpha\ge\underline\alpha_\star:=\min\{\underline\alpha,\underline\alpha_{\mathcal S,\sigma}\}\gamma$, with $\underline\alpha_{\mathcal S,\sigma}>0$ given by Lemma 4.5(i). In other words, $\alpha_{(t)}\ge\underline\alpha_\star$ for every $t$.
--   2. Every $(x^{(t)},y^{(t)})$ lies in $\mathcal S$, and for every $t$, with $C_0:=\min\{\sigma/2,1/\bar\alpha\}$ and $\eta_{(t+1)}=\eta(x^{(t+1)},y^{(t+1)})$,
--   $$
--   \zeta(x^{(t+1)})+C_0\big(\|x^{(t+1)}-x^{(t)}\|_2^2+Q_{(l(t))}\|y^{(t+1)}-y^{(t)}\|_2^2\big)\le Q_{(l(t))}\eta_{(t+1)},\tag{28}
--   $$
--   $$
--   Q(x^{(t+1)},y^{(t+1)})\le Q_{(l(t+1))}\le Q_{(l(t))}\le F(x^{(0)}).\tag{29}
--   $$
--
--   **Formalization Note** Item 1 asserts a constant $\underline\alpha_{\mathcal S,\sigma}>0$ with the property of Lemma 4.5(i) such that (a) at every iteration that updates a block, from every initial step $\tilde\alpha\in[\underline\alpha,\bar\alpha]$ and for every choice of the prox points at the trial steps $\tilde\alpha\gamma^k$, some trial passes the test with $\tilde\alpha\gamma^k\ge\underline\alpha_\star$ (finite termination), and (b) $\alpha_{(t)}\ge\underline\alpha_\star$ for all $t$. (28) and (29) are stated in the extended reals.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: ℝⁿ and ℝⁿ × ℝⁿ with the Euclidean norm and inner product → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) (Vec n) and WithLp 2 (Vec n × Vec n) (Pair n); reason: Lean convention; the same norms and inner products
--   - encoding: h : ℝⁿ → (−∞, +∞] proper lower semicontinuous, locally Lipschitz differentiable on Ω → h : Vec n → ℝ, differentiable on Ω with gradient locally Lipschitz relative to Ω; reason: h enters only through ζ = f + h and ∇h on the open set Ω; its values off Ω change no value of F or Q, no critical point and no accepted step (a trial point outside Ω fails the line-search test, since η ≤ g = 0 there and ζ ≥ 0 on dom f)
--   - encoding: subvectors x₁, …, x_N partitioning the coordinates of x, blocks i ∈ ℕ_N = {1, …, N} → a surjective blk : Fin n → Fin N with block spaces EuclideanSpace ℝ {j // blk j = i}; paper block i is index i − 1; reason: Lean convention; the same partitions into nonempty blocks
--   - encoding: extended values in (−∞, +∞] and [−∞, +∞) → EReal, with the real quotient on the finite branch of F and Q; reason: Lean convention; the same values
--   - encoding: y = prox_{αg*}(·) and x_i(α) ∈ prox_{αf_i}(·) → membership in the argmin set proxSet α φ v; reason: the prox of the convex g* is a single point, so membership and equality agree; the prox of f_i is set-valued as on p.13
--   - encoding: Q_(t) = Q(x^(t), y^(t)) (or Q(x, y)) inside the prox argument of Step 2-X → (Q x y).toReal (xStepInput); reason: it is evaluated only on dom(Q) (Theorem 4.6(ii), or (x, y) ∈ S), where the real value is Q(x, y)
--   - encoding: Step 2-X: backtrack α ← αγ from α̃(t) until the test holds → trial points p k at α̃(t)γᵏ for k ≤ j, the test failing for k < j and holding at k = j; α(t) = α̃(t)γʲ; reason: the same runs; the failed trials are recorded because Theorem 4.6(i) is about them
--   - encoding: Q_(l(t)) with l(t) = max{j ≤ t : Q_(j) = max{Q_(s) : [t − M]₊ ≤ s ≤ t}} → Qwin M x y t = ⨆ s ∈ [t − M, t], Q(x s, y s) in EReal (ℕ subtraction is [·]₊); reason: Q_(l(t)) is that maximum; the index l(t) is not needed
--   - generalization: one y-step size α := α̃_Y ∈ [α̲, ᾱ] in Algorithm 1 → a y-step size α(t) ∈ [α̲, ᾱ] that may differ between y-steps; reason: §5.1 (39) writes 'some α(k,0) ∈ [α̲, ᾱ]' and the proofs use only α(t) ∈ [α̲, ᾱ]; a constant α̃_Y is the special case, so the statement specializes to the source
--   - reading: ḡ_X > 0 given by Remark 1(i) → any gbar > 0 with g ≤ gbar on X, a parameter of Y and S; reason: Remark 1(i) only asserts that such a bound exists and every result holds for each one; η ≤ g is Fenchel–Young, not a hypothesis
--   - reading: 'Step 2-X terminates in finite steps at some α ≥ α̲⋆ … In other words, α(t) ≥ α̲⋆ for any t' → ∃ α̲_{S,σ} > 0 with the property of Lemma 4.5(i) such that, at each block iteration, every initial step in [α̲, ᾱ] and every choice of trial prox points reaches a passing trial with step ≥ α̲⋆, and α(t) ≥ α̲⋆ for all t; reason: both readings of the sentence are kept: termination for every possible execution of Step 2-X, and the bound on the recorded steps
-- source:
--   Zhou, Zhang, Li, An equivalent reformulation and multi-proximity gradient algorithms for a class of nonsmooth fractional programming, arXiv:2311.00957v2, §4, pp.17–18, Theorem 4.6

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_FracMPGA_proxSet
import Definitions.Def_FracMPGA_liftedRatio
import Definitions.Def_FracMPGA_Problem
import Definitions.Def_FracMPGA_Assumption1
import Definitions.Def_FracMPGA_setS
import Definitions.Def_FracMPGA_IsMPGARun

namespace FracMPGA

/-- **Theorem 4.6** of Zhou, Zhang, Li, arXiv:2311.00957v2, pp.17–18: suppose that Assumption 2
holds. Then
(i) Step 2-X terminates in finite steps at some `α ≥ α̲⋆`, where `α̲⋆ := min{α̲, α̲_{S,σ}} γ` with
`α̲_{S,σ} > 0` given by Lemma 4.5(i). In other words, `α(t) ≥ α̲⋆` holds for any `t ∈ ℕ`;
(ii) the sequence `{(x⁽ᵗ⁾, y⁽ᵗ⁾)}` generated by MPGA falls into `S`. For any `t ∈ ℕ`,
`ζ(x⁽ᵗ⁺¹⁾) + C₀(‖x⁽ᵗ⁺¹⁾ − x⁽ᵗ⁾‖₂² + Q_(l(t))‖y⁽ᵗ⁺¹⁾ − y⁽ᵗ⁾‖₂²) ≤ Q_(l(t)) η_(t+1)` (28),
`Q(x⁽ᵗ⁺¹⁾, y⁽ᵗ⁺¹⁾) ≤ Q_(l(t+1)) ≤ Q_(l(t)) ≤ F(x⁽⁰⁾)` (29),
where `C₀ := min{σ/2, 1/ᾱ} > 0` and `η_(t+1) := η(x⁽ᵗ⁺¹⁾, y⁽ᵗ⁺¹⁾)`.

**Formalization Note** Assumption 1 is `hA1`, Assumption 2 is `IsCompact (P.levelX (x 0))`;
`(x, y, α)` is any run of Algorithm 1 with any index sequence `I` and memory `M`, and `S` is
`P.setS (x 0) gbar αlo` for a bound `gbar` of Remark 1(i). Item (i) is stated as: there is an
`α̲_{S,σ} > 0` with the property of Lemma 4.5(i) for this `σ` such that (a) at every iteration
`t` that picks a block `r`, from every initial step `α̃ ∈ [α̲, ᾱ]` and for every choice of the prox
points `p k` at the trial steps `α̃γᵏ`, some trial `k` passes the test with `α̃γᵏ ≥ α̲⋆` (finite
termination), and (b) the recorded steps satisfy `α(t) ≥ α̲⋆` for all `t`. `Q_(l(t))` is
`P.Qwin M x y t`; (28) and (29) are stated in `EReal`. -/
theorem theorem_4_6 {n N : ℕ} (P : Problem n N) (hA1 : Assumption1 P) (αlo αhi σ γ : ℝ) (M : ℕ)
    (I : ℕ → Fin (N + 1)) (x y : ℕ → Vec n) (α : ℕ → ℝ)
    (hrun : P.IsMPGARun αlo αhi σ γ M I x y α) (hA2 : IsCompact (P.levelX (x 0)))
    (gbar : ℝ) (hgbar : 0 < gbar) (hgX : ∀ z ∈ P.levelX (x 0), P.g z ≤ gbar) :
    (∃ αS : ℝ, 0 < αS ∧
      (∀ x' y' : Vec n, pair x' y' ∈ P.setS (x 0) gbar αlo → P.Q x' y' ≤ P.F (x 0) →
        ∀ a : ℝ, 0 < a → a < αS → ∀ r : Fin N,
          ∀ p ∈ proxSet a (P.fb r) (P.xStepInput x' y' r a),
            ∀ c : ℝ, P.Q x' y' ≤ (c : EReal) →
              P.lsTest σ (c : EReal) x' y' (P.blockUpdate x' r p)) ∧
      (∀ t : ℕ, ∀ r : Fin N, I t = r.succ → ∀ α₀ : ℝ, αlo ≤ α₀ → α₀ ≤ αhi →
        ∀ p : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ {k // P.blk k = r},
          (∀ k, p k ∈ proxSet (α₀ * γ ^ k) (P.fb r) (P.xStepInput (x t) (y t) r (α₀ * γ ^ k))) →
          ∃ k : ℕ, P.lsTest σ (P.Qwin M x y t) (x t) (y t) (P.blockUpdate (x t) r (p k)) ∧
            min αlo αS * γ ≤ α₀ * γ ^ k) ∧
      (∀ t : ℕ, min αlo αS * γ ≤ α t)) ∧
    (∀ t : ℕ, pair (x t) (y t) ∈ P.setS (x 0) gbar αlo) ∧
    (∀ t : ℕ, P.zeta (x (t + 1)) + ((min (σ / 2) (1 / αhi) : ℝ) : EReal) *
        (((‖x (t + 1) - x t‖ ^ 2 : ℝ) : EReal) +
          P.Qwin M x y t * ((‖y (t + 1) - y t‖ ^ 2 : ℝ) : EReal)) ≤
        P.Qwin M x y t * P.eta (x (t + 1)) (y (t + 1))) ∧
    (∀ t : ℕ, P.Q (x (t + 1)) (y (t + 1)) ≤ P.Qwin M x y (t + 1) ∧
      P.Qwin M x y (t + 1) ≤ P.Qwin M x y t ∧ P.Qwin M x y t ≤ P.F (x 0)) := by sorry

end FracMPGA
